<a name="2"></a>
## 2. Competitive Landscape & White Space

### 2.1. Market Map

| Category | Players | AI Plan Reading | Scope Decomp | Sub Marketplace | Permit Compliance | Transaction |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Incumbent PM Platforms** | Procore, Autodesk | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ (Directory) | ✗ | ✗ |
| **AI Construction Startups** | Togal.AI, Trunk Tools, Doxel | ✓ (Partial) | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ |
| **Pure-Play Marketplaces** | PlanHub, ConstructConnect, BuildingConnected | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ (Bid board) | ✗ | ✗ |
| **AI Permit Point Solutions** | Kooply, PermitFlow | ✓ (Text only) | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ (Basic) | ✗ |
| **BuildScope AI** | **(Us)** | **✓** | **✓** | **✓** | **✓** | **✓** |

### 2.2. The White Space
No existing platform integrates all three pillars: **Machine Reading of Plans → Intelligent Subcontractor Matching → Regulatory Compliance Verification.** This is the defensible intersection we occupy.

### 2.3. Competitive Threats to Monitor
- **Togal.AI:** Exceptional computer vision for takeoff. Could attempt to build a marketplace layer.
- **Procore:** Massive installed base and a nascent marketplace. If they acquire an AI startup and integrate deeply, they become formidable.
- **Trunk Tools:** AI-native, well-funded. An "AI co-pilot for PMs" today; a pivot into procurement is plausible.

**Our Moat Timeline:** We have approximately 18-24 months to build network liquidity before any of these players can credibly integrate all three pillars. Speed of execution is our primary defense.

