## 3. Target Users & Personas

### 3.1. Dual-Sided Platform Personas

**Side A: The General Contractor / Developer (The Buyer)**
| | Paul, the GC Owner | Maria, the Compliance Director |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Company Size** | 10-50 employees | 100-500 employees |
| **Core Pain** | "I waste days manually scoping plans and calling the same five subs. I don't know if I'm overpaying." | "I have 30 active projects. If one sub lets their license lapse or misses a permit, I'm liable. I have no real-time visibility." |
| **Current Workflow** | Emails PDFs to known subs. Uses Excel for bid leveling. | Spreadsheets, Procore, and frantic phone calls. |
| **Aha Moment** | Uploading plans on Monday, having 3 qualified, competitive bids by Wednesday from subs he's never met—and saving 7% on the framing package. | Seeing a single dashboard with every sub's license status, insurance expiry, and permit acknowledgement status across all projects, updated in real time. |

**Side B: The Subcontractor (The Seller)**
| | Jose, the Electrical Sub Owner |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Company Size** | 15-40 employees |
| **Core Pain** | "I spend 20 hours a week doing manual takeoffs for bids I don't win. Finding good GCs to work with is pure word of mouth." |
| **Current Workflow** | Receives email blasts with entire 100-page plan sets. Manually finds the electrical sheets. Manually counts fixtures. Bids blind. |
| **Aha Moment** | Receiving a notification that says: "New Electrical Scope matched: 200A service upgrade, 45 branch circuits, 120 fixtures. Bid package pre-extracted. Estimated takeoff time saved: 4 hours." He bids in 30 minutes and wins a $45,000 contract. |

