<a name="4"></a>
## 4. Business Model & Pricing

### 4.1. Revenue Model Overview
BuildScope AI generates revenue from both sides of the marketplace through a blended SaaS + Transaction Fee model. This creates aligned incentives and a revenue ceiling far higher than a pure SaaS tool.

### 4.2. Detailed Pricing Tiers

**Side A: General Contractors & Developers**

| Tier | Price | Projects/Mo | Key Features |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Pro** | **$499/mo** (Annual) | Up to 5 active | AI plan analysis, scope decomposition, permit roadmap, post scopes to marketplace, compliance dashboard. |
| **Business** | **$1,299/mo** (Annual) | Up to 25 active | Everything in Pro + advanced sub management, white-labeled bid packages, code change radar, priority support. |
| **Enterprise** | **Custom** ($3k-$8k/mo) | Unlimited | Everything in Business + API access, SSO, dedicated CSM, custom integrations with Procore/Autodesk. |

**Side B: Subcontractors**
- **Free Tier:** Receive matched bid invitations. Submit bids. Manage awarded contracts and permit acknowledgements. (No cost to receive work.)
- **Sub Pro:** **$149/mo** (Annual). Advanced profile with portfolio showcase, priority placement in GC search results, instant push notifications on scope postings matching your trades, and access to historical pricing analytics for smarter bidding.
- **Marketplace Transaction Fee:** **4.5% of awarded subcontract value**, capped at $2,000 per contract, paid by the subcontractor upon contract signing. This ensures subs only pay when they win work. GCs pay zero transaction fees to post scopes.

### 4.3. Unit Economics Illustration
A single mid-size project with $500,000 in subcontracts awarded through the platform:
- **GC SaaS Revenue:** $499/mo (Pro tier, allocated across their active projects)
- **Sub Transaction Fees:** 4.5% × $500,000 = $22,500, capped at $2,000 × (number of subcontracts). For 5 subcontracts: ~$10,000 in transaction fees.
- **Total Platform Revenue for One Project:** ~$10,500.
- **Compare:** A chatbot subscription: $20/month.

