<a name="6"></a>
## 6. Functional Requirements

### 6.1. Project Intake & Plan Processing Module
- **FR-01: Multi-Format Ingestion:** Accept PDF, DWG, DXF, RVT, IFC, JPG, PNG, TIFF. Bulk upload via .zip supported.
- **FR-02: Document Classification AI:** Fine-tuned CV model classifies each sheet by type: Architectural Plan, Structural Plan, Civil Plan, MEP Plan, Title Sheet, Detail, Schedule, or Unrecognized. Confidence score displayed per sheet.
- **FR-03: Optical Character Recognition (OCR):** Extract all text from vector and raster PDFs, including handwritten notes (with low-confidence flag). Extracted text is stored as searchable metadata.
- **FR-04: Construction Symbol Detection:** CV model trained on a proprietary dataset of architectural/engineering symbols detects: walls, doors, windows, plumbing fixtures, electrical panels, HVAC diffusers, structural columns, and fire protection devices. Each detection is a structured data object with type, coordinates, and confidence score.
- **FR-05: Named Entity Recognition (NER) for Scope:** NLP model processes all extracted text from notes, schedules, and specifications to identify scope-describing phrases ("Relocate sprinkler main," "New 400A service," "Remove load-bearing wall at Gridline C").
- **FR-06: Quantity Aggregation:** Detected elements are quantified (counts, areas, linear feet) and grouped by MasterFormat division. Output is a structured JSON object representing each Scope Package.
- **FR-07: Geospatial Overlay Analysis:** On project address entry, automatically query and overlay: FEMA Flood Zone, National Register of Historic Places district, US Fish & Wildlife wetlands, state coastal zone boundaries, and local zoning district.
- **FR-08: Adaptive Project Wizard:** Dynamic questionnaire adapting based on extracted data. Minimum required fields: Project Valuation ($), Occupancy Classification (IBC Chapter 3), Construction Type (I-V), Work Type (New Construction, Alteration, Addition, Change of Use).

### 6.2. Regulatory Intelligence & Permit Engine
- **FR-09: Jurisdictional Rule Graph Database:** A versioned graph database (Neo4j) containing permit trigger logic for every supported jurisdiction. Nodes represent Scope Tags, Permits, Code Sections, and Issuing Authorities. Relationships represent conditional triggers.
- **FR-10: Deterministic Rules Engine:** The permit requirement list is generated by executing the project's extracted Scope Tags against the rule graph. Generative AI is strictly prohibited from generating the final permit list. It is only used for unstructured text interpretation.
- **FR-11: Citation Transparency & Source Linking:** Every permit recommendation includes: Permit Name, Issuing Authority, Triggering Scope Tag, and a direct hyperlink to the official, adopted municipal code section. An audit log records the exact rule version used.
- **FR-12: Fee & Timeline Estimator:** Based on jurisdiction-sourced data and anonymized historical data, provide a permit fee estimate range and a typical review timeline for each permit.

### 6.3. Subcontractor Profile & Verification Engine
- **FR-13: Identity & Business Verification:** Subcontractor registration requires business name, EIN, principal contact, and proof of business entity status.
- **FR-14: License Validation API:** Real-time integration with state licensing board databases. License number, classification, expiration date, and any disciplinary actions are verified on registration and re-verified monthly. Expired or invalid licenses immediately suspend marketplace access.
- **FR-15: Insurance & Bonding Verification:** Subcontractors upload Certificate of Insurance (COI). AI parses the COI for coverage types, limits, effective dates, and named insured. System flags expiring COIs 30 days in advance. Bonding capacity is verified via surety provider integration or manual upload with verification workflow.
- **FR-16: Work Radius & Trade Selection:** Subcontractors define their service area (by county or radius from zip code) and select their trade categories from a MasterFormat-based taxonomy.
- **FR-17: Dynamic Capacity Declaration:** Subcontractors maintain a current "Available Capacity" indicator (High, Medium, Low, At Capacity). The matching engine weights availability in its recommendations.

### 6.4. Marketplace Matching & Bidding Engine
- **FR-18: Scope Posting & Configuration:** GC can post any AI-generated Scope Package to the marketplace. Required fields: bid deadline, preferred start date, any additional notes or requirements.
- **FR-19: Intelligent Matching Algorithm:** A scoring engine ranks subcontractors for each scope based on a weighted composite score: License Match (binary pass/fail) > Geographic Fit > Performance Rating > Capacity > Specialization Match > Platform Activity.
- **FR-20: Bid Package Assembly:** Matched subcontractors receive a structured bid package containing: the AI-quantified scope of work, relevant extracted plan sheets, project timeline, and any GC notes.
- **FR-21: Blind Bidding System:** Bids are sealed until the deadline. The GC can see who has been invited and who has viewed the package, but not bid amounts.
- **FR-22: Bid Leveling Dashboard:** After the deadline, the GC sees a sortable, filterable table comparing bids: Subcontractor Name, Performance Rating, Bid Amount, Bidder Notes, and "Award" button.
- **FR-23: In-Platform Messaging:** Secure, logged messaging between GC and Sub for scope clarifications before and during bidding. System monitors for circumvention indicators (phone numbers, external emails) and flags potential ToS violations.

### 6.5. Contract, Compliance & Closeout
- **FR-24: Transaction Fee Processing:** Upon award, the 4.5% transaction fee (capped at $2,000) is calculated and charged to the subcontractor's payment method on file.
- **FR-25: Digital Subcontract Generation:** The platform auto-populates a standardized subcontract agreement template with the project details, scope of work (from the AI-generated Scope Package), contract value, and dates. Both parties e-sign via integrated e-signature provider (e.g., Dropbox Sign or DocuSign API).
- **FR-26: Compliance Ledger Activation:** Upon contract execution, the system automatically identifies the trade permits applicable to that subcontractor's scope and adds them to the project's Compliance Dashboard, with the sub assigned as "Responsible Party."
- **FR-27: Digital Permit Acknowledgement:** Assigned subcontractors receive notification to acknowledge their trade permits. They can mark permits as "In Progress" or "Obtained" (with permit number and optional document upload). All status changes are time-stamped and logged.
- **FR-28: Code Change Radar:** The system monitors the code sections cited in all active project permits. When a monitored code is amended in the project's jurisdiction, an alert is pushed to the GC and any impacted sub.
- **FR-29: Post-Project Rating System:** Upon project completion, the GC must rate each awarded subcontractor on a 1-5 star scale across four dimensions: Safety, Schedule Adherence, Quality of Work, and Communication. A composite score is calculated and displayed on the sub's profile. Subcontractors may post a single public response to any review.

