<a name="7"></a>
## 7. Non-Functional Requirements

- **NFR-01: Explainability & Grounding:** Every AI-extracted element (symbol, quantity, scope tag) must be traceable to its visual source on the original plan sheet. A "Show me" button highlights the detection's bounding box. Every permit recommendation must link to its governing code citation.
- **NFR-02: Data Privacy & Tenant Isolation:** Project data, financials, and bid information are strictly isolated between competing organizations. Enterprise customers receive dedicated database schema isolation.
- **NFR-03: Availability:** Core platform 99.9% uptime SLA. The regulatory engine and matching engine run on separate high-availability clusters.
- **NFR-04: Response Time:** Initial plan processing and scope decomposition < 2 minutes for a 50-sheet plan set. Marketplace matching results displayed in < 5 seconds after posting.
- **NFR-05: Security & Compliance:** SOC 2 Type II certification target within 12 months of launch. Data encrypted at rest (AES-256) and in transit (TLS 1.3). Full, immutable audit logging of all user actions, contract events, and data modifications.
- **NFR-06: Legal & Liability Framework:** On signup, every project creation, and every report export, users must acknowledge that BuildScope AI outputs are "AI-Generated Advisory Drafts for Professional Validation." The platform is not a licensed design, engineering, or legal service. A persistent, non-dismissible disclaimer is present in the application footer. The platform's Terms of Service include a binding arbitration clause and explicit non-circumvention obligations for marketplace participants.

