<a name="9"></a>
## 9. Data Model & Privacy

### 9.1. Core Data Entities
- **Organization:** Company name, billing plan, payment method, default jurisdiction, branding assets (for white-label).
- **User:** Name, email, role (GC_Admin, GC_ProjectManager, Sub_Owner, Sub_Estimator), associated Organization.
- **Project:** Address, valuation, occupancy type, construction type, work class, current stage, Compliance Health Score, associated PlanSet.
- **PlanSet:** Collection of uploaded `Document` objects, each with extracted metadata (OCR full text, detected symbols, confidence scores).
- **ScopePackage:** An AI-generated, GC-edited work package. Contains trade division, quantified elements, associated documents, bid deadline, status (Draft, Posted, Bidding, Awarded, Completed).
- **Bid:** Submitted by a Subcontractor on a specific ScopePackage. Contains bid amount, inclusions/exclusions, notes, and timestamp. Sealed until deadline.
- **Contract:** Generated upon award. Contains final scope, value, parties, e-signature status, and links to associated PermitRequirements.
- **SubcontractorProfile:** Extended user profile with license info, insurance, bonding, work radius, trade categories, capacity, and composite performance rating.
- **PermitRequirement:** A specific permit linked to a Project and optionally to a Contract/Sub. Status (Required, In Progress, Obtained, N/A), permit number, issuing authority, linked code citations.
- **PerformanceReview:** GC-submitted ratings and optional text review linked to a completed Contract.
- **AuditEvent:** Immutable log of all significant user and system actions.

### 9.2. Data Privacy & Governance
- **Data Ownership:** Users retain 100% ownership of all uploaded plans, project data, and proprietary information. BuildScope AI claims a limited, non-exclusive license to process data to provide the service.
- **Anonymized Data Usage:** A specific, opt-in consent is required for using anonymized, aggregated data for AI model improvement. Opt-in is incentivized but not required for core service.
- **Data Deletion Policy:** Upon subscription cancellation, project and profile data are preserved in read-only state for 90 days. During this window, users may export all data (structured CSV, PDF reports, plan files). After 90 days, all data is permanently purged via automated, audited deletion scripts.
- **Marketplace Data Firewall:** Bidding data, contract values, and performance reviews are strictly governed by role-based access. A subcontractor's bid is visible only to the GC on that specific scope, not to other subs. Proprietary pricing data is never exposed across competing GCs.

