<a name="10"></a>
## 10. UX/UI Design Specifications

### 10.1. Guiding Design Principles
- **Progressive Confidence:** The UI visually distinguishes between AI-extracted data (amber "AI-suggested" badge) and human-verified data (green "GC-confirmed" badge). Trust is built through transparency, not false certainty.
- **Source-Link Everything:** Every detected symbol, every extracted quantity, every recommended permit is a clickable element linking directly to its source: a bounding box on the plan sheet or a hyperlink to the municipal code.
- **Action-Oriented Dashboard:** The primary dashboard is not a passive data display. It is an "Action Required" feed. The user's first glance answers: "What do I need to do today?"

### 10.2. Key Screens

**Screen 1: Command Center (Post-Login Default for GCs)**
- **Top Bar:** Org name, "New Project" button (prominent, always visible), global search, notification bell with badges for: new bids received, sub acknowledgements pending, code change alerts.
- **Left Panel:** Filterable project list. Each row shows Project Name, Address, Stage Badge, and a Health Score donut chart. At-risk projects (Health Score <70) are highlighted in red and pinned to the top.
- **Main Canvas:** A "Priority Feed" showing time-sensitive items across all active projects: expiring sub insurance, pending bid deadlines, overdue permit acknowledgements, code change alerts. Items are grouped by project and sorted by urgency.

**Screen 2: The Scope Decomposition Studio (The Core Differentiator)**
- **Split-Panel Layout:**
    - **Left Panel (Plan Viewer):** High-performance PDF/DWG viewer. Toggle overlay mode to see AI detections as color-coded bounding boxes. Click any box to see extracted data and confidence score. User can "Confirm" or "Reject" any AI detection, training the model over time.
    - **Right Panel (Scope Packages):** A vertical, scrollable list of AI-generated Scope Packages, grouped by trade division. Each package card shows: Trade, Quantified Summary, Confidence Score, and buttons for "Edit," "Post to Marketplace," or "Assign Manually." Expanding a card shows the detailed quantity takeoff.
- **Action:** GC reviews, adjusts quantities, adds notes, and clicks "Post to Marketplace" on a package. A modal confirms the bid deadline and the number of matched subs who will be invited.

**Screen 3: Bid Leveling & Award Dashboard**
- **Layout:** A table view of a specific Scope Package's bids.
- **Columns:** Subcontractor Name, Composite Star Rating, Previous Projects Completed on Platform, Bid Amount, Bidder Notes, and "Award" button.
- **Interactivity:** Clicking a sub's name opens a side panel with their full profile, performance history, and reviews. The "Award" button triggers the contract generation and transaction fee processing flow.

**Screen 4: Subcontractor Mobile View (Mobile-First)**
- **Default View:** "Open Bid Invitations" feed. Each card shows a brief scope summary, GC name, project location, bid deadline, and "View Bid Package" button.
- **Bid Package View:** Structured, mobile-readable breakdown of the scope quantities and relevant plan snippets (pre-cropped by the AI).
- **Action:** A large, thumb-friendly "Submit Bid" button with amount and optional notes.
- **My Work View:** A simple list of awarded contracts with their current compliance acknowledgement status. A prominent "Confirm Permit Obtained" button for each trade permit, with camera upload for the physical permit document.

