<a name="12"></a>
## 12. Success Metrics & KPIs

### 12.1. North Star Metric
**Gross Merchandise Value (GMV) of awarded subcontracts per month.**
This single metric proves that AI scoping and marketplace matching are producing real economic activity—not vanity engagement.

### 12.2. Supporting KPIs

| Category | Metric | Target (6 Months Post-Launch) | Why It Matters |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Marketplace Liquidity** | Monthly GMV | $2.5M+ | Core proof of product-market fit. |
| **Marketplace Liquidity** | Bid response rate (invited → bid submitted) | >35% | Indicates match quality and bid-package usefulness. |
| **Marketplace Liquidity** | Median bids per posted scope | ≥3 | Competitive dynamics required for GC retention. |
| **Demand (GC)** | Paying GC logos | 40+ | Validates willingness to pay for the SaaS layer. |
| **Demand (GC)** | Scopes posted / active GC / month | ≥2 | Habit formation; platform becomes procurement workflow. |
| **Supply (Sub)** | Verified, marketplace-ready subs | 400+ across launch metros | Supply depth without which matching fails. |
| **Supply (Sub)** | Sub Pro conversion (free → paid) | >8% of active bidders | Validates premium supply-side monetization. |
| **AI Quality** | Scope Package accept rate (GC confirms without major edit) | >70% | Trust in takeoff accuracy. |
| **AI Quality** | Permit citation dispute rate | <5% of recommendations flagged incorrect | Trust in regulatory engine. |
| **Compliance** | % awarded contracts with Compliance Ledger activated | 100% (system-enforced) | Differentiator vs. pure bid boards. |
| **Compliance** | Sub permit acknowledgement within 7 days of award | >80% | Closes the compliance loop. |
| **Retention** | GC logo churn (monthly) | <4% | Proves the product is sticky beyond a trial bid. |
| **Unit Economics** | Take rate (net marketplace fees / GMV) | 2.5–4.0% blended after caps | Path to contribution-margin health. |
| **Unit Economics** | CAC payback (blended GC + Sub) | <9 months | Sustainable growth. |

### 12.3. Leading Indicators (Weekly Ops Review)
- New verified sub profiles completed
- Plan sets successfully processed end-to-end
- Time-to-first-match after scope post (P50 / P90)
- Circumvention flags (off-platform contact attempts)
- Code Change Radar alerts issued and acknowledged

