<a name="14"></a>
## 14. Risks, Assumptions & Mitigations

### 14.1. Key Assumptions
1. Mid-market GCs will trust AI-quantified scopes enough to post them for competitive bid after a short human review.
2. Subcontractors will accept a capped success fee when bid packages meaningfully reduce takeoff time.
3. State license APIs and COI parsing are reliable enough to automate most verification; edge cases can be handled with a small ops queue.
4. Concentrating on 3 metros creates enough density for ≥3 bids per scope within 6 months.
5. Deterministic regulatory graph coverage can be maintained for launch jurisdictions with a dedicated domain analyst.

### 14.2. Risk Register

| Risk | Probability | Severity | Mitigation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Marketplace cold start** (scopes posted, few/no bids) | High | Critical | ASA seeding to 200–300 verified subs before GC launch; 72-hour bid guarantee during trial with ops-assisted matching; geographic concentration. |
| **Disintermediation** (parties meet on-platform, close off-platform) | High | High | Non-circumvention ToS; messaging monitoring for contact leakage; fee structure that feels fair (cap at $2,000); value that continues post-award (compliance, ratings, future match quality). |
| **AI quantity errors erode trust** | Medium | Critical | Progressive confidence UI; mandatory GC confirm before post; "Show me" grounding to plan geometry; human-in-the-loop feedback loop into model retraining. |
| **Permit hallucination / wrong citation** | Medium | Critical | Generative AI banned from final permit list; deterministic rule graph only; every output source-linked; "Flag as incorrect" → domain expert SLA. |
| **Regulatory data decay** | High | High | Dedicated regulatory analyst; versioned graph; Code Change Radar (V2); clear advisory disclaimer and professional-validation requirement. |
| **License/insurance verification gaps** | Medium | High | Multi-source license checks; monthly re-verification; auto-suspend on expiry; manual ops escalation for non-API states. |
| **Liability from advisory outputs** | Medium | High | Persistent disclaimer; ToS + arbitration; outputs framed as drafts for professional validation; audit log of rule versions used. |
| **Incumbent response** (Procore / BuildingConnected adds AI scoping) | Medium | High | Speed to closed-loop data moat (performance + compliance graph); exclusive depth in launch metros; association partnerships. |
| **Payment / fee collection friction** | Medium | Medium | Collect payment method at Sub Pro or first award; clear fee preview before bid submit; support for dispute holds. |

### 14.3. Open Decisions (Track Explicitly)
1. Whether "Assign Manually" (known-sub path) ships in MVP or V1.5 — recommended **V1.5** so MVP pressure-tests true marketplace liquidity first, while not blocking later relationship import.
2. Whether transaction fees are charged only to subs (current plan) or split GC/sub in Enterprise deals.
3. Build vs. buy for e-signature and payout rails (Dropbox Sign / DocuSign; Stripe Connect or equivalent).

