<a name="15"></a>
## 15. Glossary

| Term | Definition |
| :--- | :--- |
| **BuildScope Loop** | The end-to-end workflow: ingest plans → decompose scopes → match & bid → award & contract → compliance → performance feedback. |
| **Scope Package** | An AI-generated, GC-editable unit of work grouped by MasterFormat trade division, including quantified takeoff and linked plan evidence. |
| **Scope Tag** | A machine-readable label extracted from plans or notes (e.g., structural shear wall, electrical panel upgrade) used for permit triggers and matching. |
| **Verifiable Ground Truth** | Permit and compliance outputs produced by a deterministic, versioned rules engine with citations—not generative free text. |
| **Regulatory Rule Graph** | The Neo4j/Neptune graph linking Scope Tags → Permits → Code Sections → Jurisdictions, with versioning and effective dates. |
| **Citation Transparency** | Every permit recommendation includes a direct link to the adopted municipal (or higher) code section that triggers it. |
| **Intelligent Matching Engine** | Scoring system that ranks verified subcontractors for a posted scope using license, geography, performance, capacity, specialization, and activity. |
| **Blind Bidding** | Sealed bid process where amounts are hidden from the GC (and other subs) until the bid deadline. |
| **Bid Leveling** | Side-by-side comparison of submitted bids with sub ratings, history, amounts, and notes to support award decisions. |
| **Compliance Ledger** | Project-level record of required permits, responsible parties (often awarded subs), statuses, and immutable acknowledgement history. |
| **Code Change Radar** | Monitoring service that watches cited code sections for amendments and alerts impacted GCs/subs (V2). |
| **Compliance Health Score** | 0–100 portfolio/project metric reflecting obtained + N/A permits versus total required permits. |
| **Closed-Loop Transaction Network** | Marketplace design where award, compliance, and performance data feed back into matching and pricing intelligence. |
| **GMV (Gross Merchandise Value)** | Total dollar value of subcontracts awarded through the platform in a period. |
| **Take Rate** | Platform marketplace fee revenue as a percentage of GMV (affected by the per-contract fee cap). |
| **Cold Start** | The two-sided marketplace problem of needing both sufficient verified subs and active GC demand simultaneously. |
| **Disintermediation / Circumvention** | Parties using the platform to meet, then completing the transaction off-platform to avoid fees. |
| **MasterFormat** | CSI numbering system for organizing construction work by division (e.g., 03 Concrete, 26 Electrical); used to structure Scope Packages. |
| **COI** | Certificate of Insurance; uploaded and parsed to verify coverage types, limits, and dates for marketplace eligibility. |
| **Progressive Confidence** | UX pattern that visually separates AI-suggested extractions from GC-confirmed data. |

